---
import { site } from '@/config/site';
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy"
  description="What the Cherry Creek website does, and does not do, with your data."
  intro="A plain description of how this website works. It is a small community site, and it is built to collect as little as possible."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      There are no accounts, forms or comment sections, so there is nothing for you to submit.
    </li>
    <li>The site sets no cookies and shows no advertising.</li>
    <li>
      It uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and measure how quickly pages load. This is
      described below.
    </li>
    <li>
      The player guide can remember which checklist steps you have ticked. That stays in your own
      browser and is never sent anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      Fonts, images and the site's own scripts are served from this site, not from other companies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens when you visit</h2>
  <p>
    Like any website, loading a page means your browser sends a request that includes your IP
    address and basic browser details. Requests to this site pass through Cloudflare, which provides
    its network security and delivery, and then reach the server that hosts the site. Either may
    keep technical logs of requests for security and troubleshooting.
  </p>

  <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Cloudflare Web Analytics
    </a>
    to understand how it is used: which pages are viewed, roughly where visits come from (such as
    the referring site and country), which kinds of browser and device are used, and how fast pages
    load.
  </p>
  <p>
    It works through a small script loaded from Cloudflare. According to Cloudflare, Web Analytics
    does not use cookies or your browser's local storage, and does not fingerprint visitors by IP
    address, browser details or other data in order to follow them. The figures are used only to
    keep the site working well. They are not used for advertising and are not sold.
  </p>
  <p>
    Content blockers that block Cloudflare's analytics script work here as usual, and the site
    functions the same without it. Cloudflare's handling of this data is covered by the
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Cloudflare privacy policy
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h2 id="storage">What is kept in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/guide">player guide</a> has a first-day checklist. If you tick a step, your
    browser saves that in its local storage so the ticks are still there next time. Nothing is saved
    until you tick something, it is never sent to this site or anyone else, and the checklist's
    reset button, or clearing your browser's site data, removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>Live server status</h2>
  <p>
    The status card asks this website's own server whether the Minecraft server is online. It shows
    only the online state, the number of players, the player limit, the game version, and how the
    number of players has changed over the last 24 hours. These are totals only. The site never
    shows or stores player names or IP addresses, and your browser never contacts the Minecraft
    server directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Copying the server address</h2>
  <p>
    The copy buttons write the server address, or a command from the guide, to your clipboard when
    you press them. The website cannot read what is on your clipboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    The{' '}
    <a href={site.mapUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      interactive map
    </a>{' '}
    and
    <a href={site.discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Discord
    </a>{' '}
    are separate services that open in a new tab. Nothing from them is embedded here. Discord has
    its own privacy policy, and playing on the Minecraft server itself is not covered by this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Ask the community administrators on{' '}
    <a href={site.discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Discord
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Page>
